- op: discuss  # 244d
  at: '2026-07-02T17:43:21Z'  # 244d
  by: agent  # 244d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 244d
  clock: 4  # 244d
  nonce: 244d  # 244d
  message: "Done via PR #389 (merged; auto-pr re-committed as 9f2fd3f629 after a tracker auto-sync commit interleaved). The Flask/FastAPI (add_url_rule/add_api_route) and Starlette (Route) route UsageContext extractors now emit one context per declared method with metadata['http_method']=<string> (spec §9), dropping metadata['methods']=[list]. Python was the sole deviant vs rust/ruby/elixir/php/swift/js. Sole internal reader (the Starlette route-symbol minter, the only reader of metadata['methods'] in the tree) reads the string; framework_patterns extracts method from decorator/call AST (extract_method), not the usage_context. Behavioral evidence (production-path analyze_python on merged dev): add_url_rule('/u', methods=['POST','PUT']) -> 2 usage_contexts with http_method POST/PUT (no 'methods' key); default '/list' -> http_method='GET'. Minted route symbols (already one per method) unchanged. core+mainstream 100% coverage; CI passed."  # 244d
